  "script": "Apple's iPhone 18 Pro has a new signature color.\n\nIt's called Dark Cherry \u2014 and nobody agrees what it looks like.\n\nWhich is odd, because we know its exact Pantone code.\n\nAnd here's the catch: Apple's most expensive iPhone ever doesn't get it.\n\nBut first \u2014 what color is this actually?\n\nEvery render you've seen leans red.\n\nBut the leaker who detailed it says those are wrong. It's purple-tinged.\n\nAnd the reports pin it to one number: Pantone 6076.\n\nPantone files that under Red-Purple. In plain terms: a dark plum.\n\nSo if you're picturing a rich red iPhone, the real one is quieter and browner than you expect.\n\nIt's still the only risk in the lineup: Silver, Dark Gray, and a Light Blue.\n\nAnd reports don't even agree Dark Gray survives.\n\nNow \u2014 that most expensive iPhone.\n\nThe foldable iPhone Ultra reportedly gets two. Silver, and a dark blue.\n\nBoth from leaked camera protectors, not the phone.\n\nA bold color is a bet. Sell millions and a miss gets absorbed \u2014 but at a reported two thousand dollars and up, it's just unsold stock.\n\nSo the risk goes where the volume is.\n\nNone of it's confirmed \u2014 and lighting changes how any color reads.\n\nSo \u2014 plum, not red. Still the one you'd pick?",
